/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 607 0 R
/E (The course starts by examining the modern data ecosystem and how it relates to running a smart and efficient data hub. Then, it shows the student how to perform the principal tasks involved in managing extracting, transforming, and loading \(ETL\) data. This course will explain the data life cycle in a Data science project. In addition, it will cover types of data, such as structured, semi-structured, and unstructured, and the different formats of data and techniques used in the ETL process. The course also covers the elementary visualization aspects needed to understand the data. It also takes the student through staging, profiling, cleansing, and migrating data.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
